<p>The Eurovision Song Contest set its 25-country final lineup in Vienna after Thursday&#x27;s second semifinal. Saturday&#x27;s final at the Wiener Stadthalle is scheduled as the contest&#x27;s 70th edition. Five countries — Spain, Ireland, the Netherlands, Slovenia and Iceland — are not taking part in protest over Israel&#x27;s participation during the war in Gaza. Spain&#x27;s prime minister, Pedro Sánchez, defended the boycott on Friday, saying Spain was &quot;on the right side of history&quot; and that silence was not an option in the face of what he called an illegal war and genocide. Israel&#x27;s entrant, Noam Bettan, reached the final with the song &quot;Michelle&quot;; his semifinal performance drew heckling, including chants of &quot;Stop the Genocide,&quot; according to the Jewish Telegraphic Agency. Protests and alternative Eurovision events have continued in Vienna, including a Friday &quot;song protest&quot; attended by several hundred people and a Saturday demonstration registered for 3,000 participants under the slogan &quot;No Stage for Genocide&quot;. Eurovision organizers have kept Israel in the contest despite months of pressure; host-city events and rehearsals proceeded ahead of the May 16 final.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/w1p7soG6DT3sskyAvidmvoGE02LF-kshkPlEoC8Yqdsg9e0m0vCARMRcn6vcndK0_hCETk0OiDQCX9r4sgTNON0gXmEF67JbGc6nZNUKiu3T-QV_3tMzWyyhPE5qR98MNimuMKgROeXyqBrXqCj7GCxl20NtgYp2Kxf0aU2CoqkdADJ0FyQQ05rIl3_X9ufYqCqK0pxSztEJa5NwRCG7Ubc1bmoNhQO_gcafhVQ' alt='Noam Bettan, Israel&#x27;s representative at the 2026 Eurovision Song Contest, performs the song &quot;Michelle&quot; during the contest&#x27;s first semifinal.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Reduced field: At 35 participating countries, the 2026 contest has the smallest roster since 2004.</li><li>Audience scale: Eurovision is described by organizers and broadcasters as the world&#x27;s biggest live televised music spectacle, typically reaching more than 150 million viewers.</li><li>Artist campaign: More than 1,000 artists signed a boycott call over Israel&#x27;s presence in the contest, with Peter Gabriel, Brian Eno and Paul Weller listed among signatories in German coverage.</li><li>Vote concerns: Some coverage cited suspicions of televoting manipulation around the contest, while Israel denied allegations that it had rigged the Eurovision vote.</li></ul><blockquote>There was booing at the beginning, but a second passed and immediately I felt a huge wave of love and support - Noam Bettan</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pedro Sánchez, Spain&#x27;s prime minister: Sánchez framed the withdrawal as a reflection of Spain&#x27;s commitments to human rights and international law, saying RTVE&#x27;s non-participation was &quot;both consistent and necessary: to stand up against injustice.&quot; (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260515-eurovision-boycott-sanchez-says-silence-is-not-an-option-in-face-of-illegal-war-genocide/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li><li>European Broadcasting Union: Eurovision chief Martin Green responded to criticism of Israel&#x27;s inclusion by saying music can show that another world is possible. (<a href='https://www.gp.se/kultur/eurovision-chefen-martin-green-om-kontroverserna-kring-israel.e0166407-bc96-4988-b5d6-0a162a02dd20'>Göteborgs-Posten</a>)</li><li>Noam Bettan, Israel&#x27;s entrant: Bettan said he believed non-Israeli spectators were among those moved by &quot;Michelle,&quot; and that online responses helped him focus beyond the hostile reaction in the hall. (<a href='https://www.jta.org/2026/05/14/israel/noam-bettan-says-he-is-tuning-out-stop-the-genocide-chants-as-he-heads-into-eurovision-final'>Jewish Telegraphic Agency</a>)</li><li>Austria&#x27;s Young Greens: The youth Green movement publicly welcomed Bettan and said boycotting Israel&#x27;s Eurovision participation and harassing Israeli artists would not free Palestine but would contribute to a hostile environment for Jews in Europe. (<a href='https://www.jta.org/2026/05/15/global/amid-eurovision-tensions-israelis-find-allies-in-austrias-youth-green-party-and-a-cafe'>Jewish Telegraphic Agency</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/eurovision-final-lineup-confirmed-after-5-countries-packing-132981330'>The Eurovision final lineup is confirmed after 5 more countries are sent packing</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/eurovision-finalists-tune-boycotting-spain-digs'>Eurovision finalists tune up as boycotting Spain digs in</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/14/world/eurovision-israel-boycotts-china.html'>Glitz and Boycotts at Eurovision</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-05-15/why-eurovision-may-become-irrelevant-again.html'>Why Eurovision may become irrelevant again</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/15/2026/five-european-nations-contest-israels-participation-in-eurovision'>Five European nations contest Israel’s participation in Eurovision</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c0e2g5y9wyeo'>Why is Ireland not taking part in this year&#x27;s Eurovision?</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/9fb805d9-d8e6-452a-8b80-b16820d36c0a'>Israel’s Eurovision role triggers deep split in contest</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.expressen.se/noje/musik/landerna-som-bojkottar-eurovision-song-contest-ebus-svar/'>Länderna som bojkottar Eurovision song contest – EBU:s svar</a> - expressen.se</li><li><a href='https://www.lvz.de/medien/tv-programm-in-boykottlaender-statt-esc-WMDCRJJBOJCK3L6NUUKQD6XTBQ.html'>Boykott statt Eurovision: Diese Shows senden die betroffenen Länder</a> - lvz.de</li><li><a href='https://www.impartialreporter.com/news/26111372.5-countries-boycotting-eurovision-2026/'>Which countries are boycotting Eurovision 2026? See the 5 no